# DI-04 / DI-07: correction-authorisation trust root. A change to any of these needs review by a code owner.
#
# The trust root (server/lib/refresh/trustRoot.js) compares PROTECTED_FILES, the whole static import closure of
# CORRECTION_ENTRY_POINTS (66 modules today, computed at check time) and package.json / package-lock.json with
# `main`. The patterns below cover every directory that closure reaches, so a change anywhere it can grow into
# is owned too. Keep them in step with the closure (trustRoot.test.js lists it).
#
# THE OWNER MUST NOT BE THE IDENTITY AGENTS USE. GitHub never lets a pull request's author satisfy a code-owner
# review, and today agents author PRs as @rhys-daviies. Until a second, human-held account (docs/
# CORRECTION_GOVERNANCE_SEPARATION.md §2) replaces or joins the owner below and a ruleset requires code-owner
# review, this file documents intent and enforces nothing.
/.github/                                        @rhys-daviies
/.github/CODEOWNERS                              @rhys-daviies
/shared/                                         @rhys-daviies
/server/db/                                      @rhys-daviies
